                <pb facs="0293" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">494.11/69: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-11T18:00:00-05:00">March 11, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Your 56, March 10, noon. Department assumes that Japanese inquiry relates to
                    claims arising in your consular district. If so Department <pb facs="0294"
                        n="290" xml:id="pg290"/> has no objection to your furnishing informally the
                    information requested provided it is made clear that other cases of which you
                    have no knowledge may have arisen and also that the amounts indicated are not
                    necessarily final in all cases.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
